From: Alex Lennon <ajlennon@dynamicdevices.co.uk>
Subject: [PATCH] drm: bridge: sec-dsim: enable command clocks before panel prepare

The NXP sec-dsim atomic enable sequence prepares a directly attached panel
before enabling the escape and byte clocks. Panel prepare sends the HX8279-D
initialization over the DSI low-power command path, so its first packet header
remains in the controller FIFO and times out.

Enable the DSIM clocks after the PLL, D-PHY and FIFO are configured but before
drm_panel_prepare(). This matches the SanTech ST1010 power-on requirement to
send initialization while MIPI is in LP11. Leave the existing call removed so
the clocks are configured exactly once.

---
 drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/sec-dsim.c | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/sec-dsim.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/sec-dsim.c
@@ -1281,6 +1281,9 @@ static void sec_mipi_dsim_bridge_atomic_enable(struct drm_bridge *bridge,
 	/* initialize FIFO pointers */
 	sec_mipi_dsim_init_fifo_pointers(dsim);
 
+	/* Panel prepare sends LP commands and therefore needs DSIM clocks. */
+	sec_mipi_dsim_config_clkctrl(dsim);
+
 	/* prepare panel if exists */
 	if (dsim->panel) {
 		ret = drm_panel_prepare(dsim->panel);
@@ -1290,9 +1293,6 @@ static void sec_mipi_dsim_bridge_atomic_enable(struct drm_bridge *bridge,
 		}
 	}
 
-	/* config esc clock, byte clock and etc */
-	sec_mipi_dsim_config_clkctrl(dsim);
-
 	/* enable panel if exists */
 	if (dsim->panel) {
 		ret = drm_panel_enable(dsim->panel);
-- 
